3767-The first symbolic attempt exposed a real prover issue rather than a program bug: a `Val` constrained by an “is integer” predicate is not automatically re-sorted to K’s `Int`, and an unconstrained frame map also admitted impossible closure-cell branches. I’m tightening the plain-frame invariant and adding a small verification-only integer projection that is identity on every concrete `Int`; this lets the proof stay universal over `ValSeq` while preserving the `List[int]` precondition.
